  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: Why is it necessary to choose quadrats from random locations?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: As the number of individuals of any particular species will vary
    from one area to another, selecting random sample areas gives more accurate results.
  options:
  - So that we can cover the maximum ground for the study.
  - The number of individuals of a particular species varies from place to place
    within the same area.
  - To take a more accurate count, as the number of individuals may be the same in
    closely-placed quadrats.
  - None of the above
  correctOptionIndex: 1
